<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33908" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">părŏchus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάροχος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a purveyor</i>, a
			person who, for a certain sum, furnished travelling magistrates with
			necessaries, as beds, hay, straw, salt, etc. (pure Lat. copiarius).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				13, 2, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1, 5,
			46</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>an
			entertainer</i>, <i>host</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2,
				8, 36</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
